{"title":"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4721a39060a6d72daa278cc3d62a5ca459b3ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$156\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" />. Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is equilateral, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is a chord on the circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92e51b1662dd50636adb80d951997fc59fa583fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA = 4\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"21\" />, and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is outside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. What is the side length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/1/3811fccad02a654a0b8d7fc33e3d44ae36f58289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 4\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 12 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"415\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The formula for the area of a circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e89ed1c5456915b4e95e0c8a11257ac5ed3d32c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi r^2$\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> so the radius of this circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/e/24e4048c3483c17570042651b3f157849942f594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{156}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ffd2e1e416d1ac5d1ccc5720512b592110660.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA=4\\sqrt{3}=\\sqrt{48} &lt; \\sqrt{156}, A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"233\" height=\"23\" /> must be in the interior of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c79ddff6b45c6ad853d03d6231fdf0fba5ededb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O.$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03fe10542785e49de90d325a8bb86d13462ffd6a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(3mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(11pt)); dotfactor=3;  real r=sqrt(156); pair A=(0,sqrt(48)), B=(-3,sqrt(147)), C=(3,sqrt(147)); pair O=(0,0); pair X=(0,7sqrt(3)); path outer=Circle(O,r); draw(outer); draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(O--X); draw(O--B);  pair[] ps={A,B,C,O,X}; dot(ps);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,SE); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,S); label(&quot;$X$&quot;,X,N); label(&quot;$s$&quot;,A--C,SE); label(&quot;$\\frac{s}{2}$&quot;,B--X,N); label(&quot;$\\frac{s\\sqrt{3}}{2}$&quot;,A--X,NE); label(&quot;$\\sqrt{156}$&quot;,O--B,SW); label(&quot;$4\\sqrt{3}$&quot;,A--O,E); [/asy]\" width=\"358\" height=\"378\" /></center>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the side length of the triangle, the unknown value, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/620ba336cf9c7a8c7298923c5201c6f9c59e2970.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OX \\perp BC.$\" width=\"86\" height=\"12\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is equilateral, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cb819d89c4cec8d49a75538de1ab1904f9c4375.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX=\\frac{s}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"67\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84ce4dc80ff50ead1d48bbbfaaade620cb0efc0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX=\\frac{s\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"43\" /> We are given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/4/8e4f10ca7798b3119ce0607e1b1ba868123fc75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO=4\\sqrt{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> Use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> and solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09d9c01a214955f96b174391be96b26abf545cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"8\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/468dc818299e27b2804ce95f974515e503a4c540.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (\\sqrt{156})^2 &amp;= \\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right)^2 + \\left( \\frac{s\\sqrt{3}}{2} + 4\\sqrt{3} \\right)^2\\\\ 156 &amp;= \\frac14s^2 + \\frac34s^2 + 12s + 48\\\\ 0 &amp;= s^2 + 12s - 108\\\\ 0 &amp;= (s-6)(s+18)\\\\ s &amp;= \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 6} \\end{align*}\" width=\"277\" height=\"187\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the same diagram as Solution 1 and label the side length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Using congruent triangles, namely the two triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6af3c7e2f2403f2fa92d2d1d20861cb9354e0e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BOA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e2d97829369bc06782c17988a22533979294d85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle COA$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/e/c3ee988dd8e8763d2fdba5740e831853ff14f943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAO = \\angle CAO \\implies \\angle BAO = \\frac{360^\\circ-60^\\circ}{2} = 150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"412\" height=\"39\" />. From this, we can use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>, to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/39138561e4aec938a4f5b4594408d632bc8101d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s^2 + (4 \\sqrt{3})^2 - 2 \\times s \\times 4 \\sqrt{3} \\times - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = (2 \\sqrt{39})^2\\]\" width=\"361\" height=\"41\" /> Simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f41e76300e27bf883a4b5193a96636fcfffc8f97.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s^2 + 12s + 48 = 156 \\implies s^2 + 12s - 108 = 0\\]\" width=\"353\" height=\"16\" /> We can factor this to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/6/a6656760af5ff81b27a2ebe5e02d278bba7f0b98.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-6)(x+18)\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" /> Lengths must be non-negative, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/8/ac8a9cb7dadbb8ebe7303b5b5e8214059fbb7efd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"56\" height=\"30\" />\n~bryan gao\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FQO-0E2zUVI?t=906\">https://youtu.be/FQO-0E2zUVI?t=906</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B\">2010 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017145550\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 268/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6928/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.724      1 -total\n 60.68%    7.721      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.20%    4.861      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8999:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017145550 and revision id 219003. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}